Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["ExportLaTeXBundle", "ObjectName",
 CellID->305156169,ExpressionUUID->"f48e129e-e9a8-432f-ab24-ed5c6d6c73e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["\t", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
  "f9f85db3-e638-40f3-a4e9-2dce157d812f"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["ExportLaTeXBundle",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/ExportLaTeXBundle"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"notebook", ",", " ", "\"\<directory\>\""}], "]"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"af3e22a5-c1bf-4ac8-9921-c9648bb0dbf5"],
 " \[LineSeparator]writes the notebook out as a LaTeX paper in the given \
directory, together with every file the paper needs to compile: each figure \
its \\includegraphics commands name, each .bib its preamble declares, and \
\[LongDash] where a local pdfLaTeX is found \[LongDash] the .bbl, since arXiv \
runs LaTeX but not BibTeX. The result is a directory that tars into an arXiv \
submission, where \
[ExportLaTeXDocument](paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/\
ExportLaTeXDocument) writes the .tex alone.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["ExportLaTeXBundle",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/ExportLaTeXBundle"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"notebook", ",", " ", "\"\<directory\>\"", ",", " ", "opts"}], 
    "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "616dd940-28f4-463f-9b46-d0a0a6774a29"],
 " \[LineSeparator]uses the given options.",
 Cell["\t", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"82c83a93-7cf6-408e-98ff-2a00a0a2b55f"]
}], "Usage",
 CellID->251600657,ExpressionUUID->"0ee15a9e-c97a-4418-bf93-8e7367af24bc"],

Cell["\<\
A file the paper names that is not on disk is reported and never omitted \
silently \[LongDash] and never evaluated either: the format and the size an \
\\includegraphics assumes cannot be recovered from the notebook, and guessing \
them would be guessing at the author's compile route.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8d24e9f1-39b5-4478-aa0d-8333258e4fa5"],

Cell["\<\
No compiled PDF is included. arXiv excludes .pdf and .ps from a source \
upload, so the optional LaTeX run happens in a scratch copy of the bundle and \
only the .bbl is brought back \[LongDash] which is also what keeps the .aux \
and .log out of it.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d130fdd6-df37-451b-962a-3315157b1ce3"],

Cell["\<\
\"SourceDirectory\" is where the paper's own files are looked for, and \
defaults to the notebook's directory. \"Name\" is the base name of the .tex, \
which is \\jobname for a paper that declares its bibliography as \
\\jobname.bib. \"Bibliography\" -> False skips the LaTeX run.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f707ed4f-e147-4396-b827-468c97849bfa"],

Cell["\<\
A paper whose bibliography is written into the .tex as a thebibliography \
declares no .bib and needs no .bbl, so no LaTeX run is attempted for it.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bf10ea14-98cc-427a-86b2-9c8f7def32a3"],

Cell["\<\
The result is an Association of the target directory, the files written, and \
the names the paper used that could not be resolved.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"935196d2-0b38-409e-bef0-eeea2cb90b06"]
}, Open  ]],

